/-!
# `Work.MotAS.AsRhoDefs` — the dehomogenised `0`-th component of the AS inverse map on the ruling

The target of `Work.MotAS.asPhi2_rho_ne_zero` is the nonvanishing of the vector

`kleinRAS a b g (fun j => W j / W 0)`,  `W = asRuleQW a b g c RatFunc.X`,

over the field `RatFunc ↥(twistFieldAS D (fAS 𝕜))`.  By `Work.MotAS.asRulingEval` the vector
`kleinRAS a b g W` is *proportional* to `c = asY0`, so (as `c 0 = 1`) the whole statement is
equivalent to the nonvanishing of its `0`-th component.  That component is, as a function of the
curve point `c` and the ruling parameter `t`, the degree-`6` form

`V₀(c,t) = kleinRAS0 a b g (asRuleQW a b g c t)`.

This file records `V₀` as an honest polynomial in five variables over a commutative ring (with the
ruling parameter specialised to `1`), together with the five *dehomogenised* AS Pfaffians
`asAffP k a b g = kleinPAS a b g (1, X₀, X₁, X₂, X₃) k`, i.e. the equations of the affine chart
`c 0 = 1` of the twisted Klein curve.

The single mathematical input that the final proof of `asPhi2_rho_ne_zero` needs from this file is
that `V₀` does **not** vanish identically on that affine curve, i.e. that `V₀` is not in the
radical of the ideal generated by the five dehomogenised Pfaffians (equivalently: that there is a
point of the affine curve — over some field extension — at which `V₀ ≠ 0`).  Verified numerically
(e.g. at `a = b = g = 1` over `𝔽₅` the point `(1,4,1,4,4)` lies on the affine curve and
`V₀ = 3 ≠ 0` there).
-/

open MvPolynomial

namespace Work.MotAS

/-- The `0`-th component of the cubic form `kleinRAS (asRuleQW · 1)` of the ruling, i.e. the
proportionality factor of `kleinRAS` on the ruling line at the ruling parameter `t = 1`, as a
degree-`6` polynomial in the five coordinates. -/
noncomputable def asRhoPoly (K : Type) [CommRing K] (a b g : K) : MvPolynomial (Fin 5) K :=
  kleinRAS0 (MvPolynomial.C a) (MvPolynomial.C b) (MvPolynomial.C g)
    (asRuleQW (MvPolynomial.C a) (MvPolynomial.C b) (MvPolynomial.C g)
      (fun i => MvPolynomial.X i) (1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 5) K))

/-- The five AS Pfaffians dehomogenised at the affine chart `c 0 = 1`. -/
noncomputable def asAffP (K : Type) [CommRing K] (a b g : K) (k : Fin 5) :
    MvPolynomial (Fin 5) K :=
  kleinPAS (MvPolynomial.C a) (MvPolynomial.C b) (MvPolynomial.C g)
    (fun i => if i = 0 then (1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 5) K) else MvPolynomial.X i) k

end Work.MotAS
